hi  everyone welcome to the session on  google trust we are part of the google  cloud trust team  and we work closely with our customers  to ensure that you can  confidently use our products and our  technologies from a trust perspective  specifically today will focus on  privacy security and compliance  both industry best practices and  regulatory mandates  data integrity operational transparency  and user control in this session we'll  walk you through  how our trust teams engages with  customers  to achieve this we have a very simple  agenda for you today  the introduction is really focused on  trust in the cloud  and how that manifests in everything  that we do  we'll then delve into the three c's and  you're probably wondering  what the three c's are without giving  too much away  we hope that we've piqued your curiosity  and then we'll wrap by sharing some  resources  on where you can find more information  about google cloud compliance privacy  and security by way of introduction  my name is ronnie irbis i lead the  enterprise trust  team at google cloud and as a team we're  responsible  for helping our enterprise customers in  highly regulated  industries with their compliance  and privacy and trust related  assessments and  implementations we work closely with our  customers globally  and additionally we assist with  customer-led audits  regulator audits which includes data  center audits  i am here with my colleague ruchi karana  and ruchi leads the google's security  risk  program and this program is focused on  ensuring  the ongoing privacy and security  of our customer data she collaborates  with many of  our highly regulated cloud  enterprise customers on engagements  related to trust security  audit and compliance  as i had mentioned i am part of the  trust team  at google and our house is built on  four pillars the first pillar is around  protection data security is  the foremost in everything that we do  it is part of our dna you've already  heard probably about our layers of  security controls our firewall  virtual private cloud service controls  cloud armor iem identity and  access management with policy  intelligence  and now the cloud security command  center premium  with security health analytics to help  with compliance and misconfiguration  detection  we've delivered additional  security functionality with recapture  enterprise and web  risk where we prevent bot attacks fake  account  creation fraud malware phishing  all that could impact our customers and  our customers end users  our second pillar really is around  transparency  the road to trust has to be built  through transparency  and that transparency has to be based on  accurate and on-demand information  and we have built and delivered features  to our customers like  access transparency access approvals  third-party key management specifically  for that reason  products that enforce customer control  which leads us to our third point  control  we live by the principle that our  customers  own their data we don't  you can access it take it out at any  time  we have built and equipped our customers  with tools and technology to manage  access  and protect their data and last but not  least is  enterprise compliance we've built  world-class capabilities to  enable and facilitate our customers  compliance  with the fast range of regulatory bodies  around the world  we invest in achieving and maintaining  our regulatory certifications and  attestations for all of our products  across all of our data centers globally  so for the purpose of today's  presentation we'll be looking at  trust through the lens of our enterprise  customer engagements  and for ease of discussion let's talk  about it from  one a compliance perspective to  a commitment perspective and three the  collaboration  angle starting with compliance  our customer-centric approach to  compliance has really enabled us to view  compliance with a much  wider perspective so if you look at the  pyramid  in front of you compliance of google  cloud  we deliver foundational certifications  as well as industry specific  certifications  that addresses multiple industry  segments such as  public sector healthcare financial  services to name a few  over the foundation is compliance in  google cloud  we deliver a comprehensive set of  capabilities  to help customers ensure that their  google cloud workloads  are always compliant compliance toolkits  where we deliver a very diverse range of  self-service compliance tools to help  our customers  assess act and comply  with their regulatory requirements  so our customers and regulators expect  as they should  independent verification of our security  privacy and compliance controls and  google undergoes  independent third-party audits on a  regular basis  to provide this assurance this means  that an independent auditor  has examined the controls present  in our data centers our infrastructure  and in operations our certifications  include widely recognized and  internationally accepted independent  security standards including  iso 27001 for security controls  2717 27017  for cloud security 27018  for cloud privacy as well as soft one  soft to stock 3  and these certifications help us meet  the demands of  industry standards also such as csa star  pci dss and many other regional  standards as well  and we continue to expand the list of  our certifications globally  to assist our customers with their very  dynamic  compliance landscape and  here's a list of some of the regulatory  authorities that  we've engaged both unilaterally and with  our industry peers  and with our customers we're also  working on  more compliance products and toolings to  help our customers streamline  and automate their compliance process  with their regulators  so moving on i'm going to hand this over  to ruchi who's going to talk about  the second c in the trust journey that  we're taking you on  over taruchi thanks rani for the  wonderful introduction  and the summary on the compliance piece  now let's talk about commitments  major part of the commitments is  transparency  a cloud provider should detail how it  operates  at google we are committed towards  providing you transparency  of our security design choices via  multiple artifacts  a few recent examples include our  overall infrastructure security  encryption at rest  and encryption and transit across our  platforms  when you have these types of detailed  documentations  you can make the decision yourself to  determine  if what we are doing for security and  privacy  is adequate  next a cloud provider should provide  binding commitments on how it will  operate  and handle your data internally these  areas of commitment should include  things like processing restrictions  business continuity  data deletion data incident notification  process  subprocessor list and other security  measures  at google we are transparent and  committed towards  all of these areas you can easily find  these commitments  on our data processing security terms  page  now let's talk about the third c that is  collaboration  and it's one of the most important c of  the trust  talking about collaboration at google we  offer  a suite of services when it comes to  collaborations  to start with we have a huge team of  specialists  who will help you to understand google's  grc posture  we offer workshops and one-to-one  sessions  with grc gurus an example would be  understanding compliance lifecycle at  google  secondly we offer free access to  google's third-party audit reports  which radi mentioned earlier such as iso  sock  fedramp and others thirdly  our teams work on multitude of security  and compliance  collaterals to help you understand  and address common security risks  last but not the least we are dedicated  towards supporting your due diligence  or third party risk efforts in the form  of facilitating your cyber security risk  assessments  next let me talk through collaboration  through audit rights  at google we are committed to meet your  regulatory  and contractual requirements of right to  audit  we offer all regulated customers  right to assess us on security controls  moreover we also offer your customers  or end users transitive right to audit  google's services and organizational  controls  secondly we understand that your  operations  may extend beyond a certain region so  we offer the right to inspect a google  data center  for physical and environmental security  controls  in whichever region you are operating  thirdly we are committed to support any  audits  that may be requested by our regulators  what we have found is that transparency  is the key when it comes to working with  regulators  and our teams will work with you and  support any request  with the utmost transparency  and finally we also offer pooled audits  where multiple institutions can pull  together as one group  to audit google services and  organizational controls  this approach benefits both google and  google customers  in terms of time resources level of  effort  and audit depths to give you an example  of pooled audits  google is committed towards supporting  ccag pooled audits for european  financial institutions these financial  institutions are required to conduct a  comprehensive risk assessment  of their cloud providers to comply with  their regulatory obligations  from regulatory bodies such as eba or  baffin etc  to optimize on time and cost of the  effort  these european financial institutions  work together as a team  in 2019 we supported google's  first ccag audit audit planning and  execution took over six months from both  the sites  auditors collected over 800 plus  documents  and 175 plus googlers from  24 different teams were involved in  supporting this audit  this shows how much committed we are to  pooled audits  and 2020 pooled audits is also coming  soon  now when we talk about auditable cloud  universe or any security program per se  there are many  areas of responsibility starting from  the base layer  of securing infrastructure to going up  in the stack of securing the network  securing data securing applications or  managing identities and access  there are also like ongoing processes  for security operations  governance risk and compliance  management  at google we provide capabilities to  audit  all the domains that are relevant for  your business operations  we have a global team who can support  you in any region  be it america's europe japan asia  pacific  we collaborate with local teams on both  policy and industry  to better understand the regulations  that you are subject to  so that we can provide the highest level  of services  when it comes to facilitating these  audit requests  now here are some additional resources  for you to learn more about  google's security compliance and trust  posture  and offerings thank you so much for  listening to us today hope you learned  about how google cloud is building trust  through compliance commitment and  customer collaborations  thank you thank you so much  you

